    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d347">

                <pb facs="0326" n="318" sameAs="frus:frus1937v04/pg318"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/10013: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Swatow</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Ketcham</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Swatow</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-09-10T17:00:00+08:00">September 10, 1937—5
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received September 10—2:09 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Referring to my telegrams September 6, 8 and 9,<anchor n="17" xml:id="d347-f1"/>
                    describing shelling and bombing of Swatow and subsequent meeting of the Consular
                    Corps, I feel that bombardment of city which contains nothing of military
                    importance excepting for a few machine gun <pb facs="0327" n="319"
                        xml:id="pg319"/> emplacements, constitutes a grave danger to American and
                    other foreign lives and property to say nothing of Chinese civilian population
                    which latter has already suffered considerable casualties. Japanese attacks were
                    without warning and Mayor’s office and police headquarters both purely civilian
                    organizations situated in center of city were deliberately singled out for air
                    bombing attacks and both were struck. American and foreign homes and business
                    interests are scattered throughout the city particularly near the water front
                    and any bombarding or shelling seriously endangers them. Standard Oil Company as
                    reported in my telegram September 9 [<hi rendition="#italic">8</hi>], 5 [<hi
                        rendition="#italic">3</hi>] p.m.<anchor n="18" xml:id="d347-f2"/> received
                    bomb and shell fragments in attack of September 8th and a devastating fire could
                    easily have occurred. Two bombs struck within 2 or 3 hundred yards of Company’s
                    property. In view of the foregoing it is respectfully suggested that Department
                    and Embassy may consider it desirable to protest against continued bombardment
                    Swatow.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Ketcham</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
